# do not delete me
#
# Git tracks files, not directories, so this directory would vanish from
# the next clone without a file in it. This is that file. It ignores
# nothing on purpose — see `keepMarker` in schemas/cat-harness.ts.
#
# docs-source/
# The docs graph's own SOURCE: one directory per generated page
# (`<group>-<slug>/`), holding its authored blocks (`.md`), its
# content-object manifests (`.ts`, `prose` and `webpage`) and their
# generated `.jsonld`. `gen-docs-pages.ts` renders each into the page beside
# it (`docs/<group>/<slug>.md`); Jekyll excludes this directory
# (`_config.yml`), so a block is never published as a page of its own. Moved
# here from `content/docs/` on 2026-10-09 (owner: "move content/docs into
# docs/"), so the docs subgraph carries its own source and a mount of `docs`
# brings it.
